  "evaluation": "All three correctly classify the disagreement as genuine: both findings concern vitamin D and depressive symptoms, and neither study provides an explicit underpowering signal that would dissolve the conflict. A gives a concise, accurate population-based explanation and captures the other relevant differences. C provides fuller supporting detail, but its description of Study A participants as “non-depressed” overstates the exclusion of severe depression. B is also defensible: dose, form, delivery, and duration differ substantially, although pregnancy-specific enrollment is arguably the more salient distinction. All three include an unrequested rationale field.",
  "ranking": ["A", "C", "B"]
}
